# grey prose/en/wire/values · signer lane-A is not admitted
bound-lock/1 about="The kernel never looks inside a value; each value has its own grammar, one function each in `topos/wire`. An alphabet is members apart by `|`, with `\\|` and `\\\\` escaped, `not:` before them to forbid and `none` for no member at all. Fields are `key=value` members of an alphabet, parted at the first `=`. A scope is steps apart by `/`, every step kept. A region is `name@resolution`, its resolution digits or `*`. A requirement is `name@range`, parted at its last `@`, so a scoped name keeps its own. Each function reads its text and writes it back canonical, and what it writes reads back the same." at=witness:a-requirement-the-manifests-parsed-by-hand by=lane-A epoch=1 form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/wire/values sig="ed25519:era1:GoOd+0Kiv6LfglcXbJXmVoHgJd+FM9fgqKKcTKkVlTkT8WQRTVdndpcyXE5PY15nL7koqXdPD2ls6RR4UM5NAA==" value=lock
# grey prose/en/wire/values/heading · signer lane-A is not admitted
